title: c2c Codex install sets unsupported 10s SessionEnd hook timeout
updated_at: "2026-09-29T23:33:22Z"
---
Observed: Codex reports "clamping SessionEnd hook timeout to 3s" because the c2c-managed block in ~/.codex/config.toml writes timeout = 10 for the SessionEnd command hook c2c hook codex. Expected: c2c should generate a SessionEnd timeout that Codex accepts, such as 3 seconds or the documented default, without a warning. Acceptance: update the Codex hook installation or template to stop writing 10 for SessionEnd; keep UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse, and SessionStart timeout behavior unchanged; add or update coverage so repeated installation does not restore the unsupported value and the generated config is warning-free.